---

<DocsLayout
  current="changelog"
  title="Changelog"
  description="What changed in Agentry, by release: 0.3.0 (lanes, agentry mem), v0.2 with the docs site, back to the initial v0.1 line."
  eyebrow="Reference · Changelog"
  lede="A hand-authored record of what changed, newest first. It tracks releases, not commits, so it leans toward what changed for you. The repo's CHANGELOG.md has every entry."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 class="prose__h">0.3.0 — 2026-11-05</h2>
    <p>
      Agentry 0.3 turns the plugin into a harness for a repo's own board. <code>/agentry:exec</code> builds a
      task whose contract is already written, in its own git worktree. A second agent checks the work against
      the acceptance, and <code>/agentry:merge</code> lands it only past your repo's gate. Each step is recorded
      in a ledger, so a cold session can resume. <code>/agentry:init</code> learns the board you have or
      scaffolds one, and <code>/agentry:start</code> and <code>/agentry:close</code> open and end a session the
      same way each time. The <code>agentry</code> command does the mechanical work; the plugin starts no server
      and ships no hooks. Memory is now <code>agentry mem</code>, over the same files as before, and the plugin's
      own servers are gone.
    </p>
    <p>
      Restart Claude Code after updating. <code>agentry --version</code> prints the build you are running.
      The repo's <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> lists what to change when upgrading from 0.2.
    </p>

    <h3 class="prose__h prose__h--sub">Added</h3>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><strong>Your board, as <a href={withBase("docs/lanes/")}>lanes</a></strong> — <code>/agentry:exec</code> builds a contracted task in its own worktree with a builder, an independent verifier and your repo's gate; <code>/agentry:merge</code> lands it.</li>
      <li><strong>Setup and sessions</strong> — <code>/agentry:init</code> learns your board or scaffolds one; <code>/agentry:new</code>, <code>/agentry:board</code>, <code>/agentry:start</code>, <code>/agentry:close</code> and <code>/agentry:ask</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>The <code>agentry</code> CLI</strong> — <code>board</code>, <code>lane</code>, <code>mem</code>, <code>draft</code>, <code>run</code> and <code>lock</code>, on the Bash tool's PATH while the plugin is enabled.</li>
      <li><strong>Work already on main</strong> — <code>agentry lane merge &lt;id&gt; --resolve landed</code> closes a verified lane whose commits reached main another way, found by patch.</li>
      <li><strong>Time limits and locks</strong> — <code>agentry run --limit &lt;dur&gt;</code> stops a command's whole process group at the limit; named locks share a slot across worktrees.</li>
      <li><strong>Workflow presets</strong> — <code>exec.preset</code> (<code>lean</code>, <code>standard</code>, <code>strict</code>) sets how much checking a lane gets.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="prose__h prose__h--sub">Changed</h3>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><strong><a href={withBase("docs/memory/")}>Memory</a> is the <code>agentry mem</code> CLI</strong> — the memory MCP server is gone and the plugin starts no server. Existing stores read unchanged. A lane's close writes its episode in one call.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="prose__h prose__h--sub">Removed</h3>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><strong>All plugin hooks</strong>, the primer among them. Their work moved into the commands.</li>
      <li><strong>The run-state server</strong> from v0.2. <code>/agentry:go</code> and its steps write the spec, plan and task files as plain files under <code>.agentry/work/</code>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="prose__h">v0.2</h2>
    <p>
      The release that adds a multi-page docs site and a self-eval harness to the
      conductor-plus-memory core.
    </p>

    <h3 class="prose__h prose__h--sub">Added</h3>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><strong>The docs &amp; marketing site</strong> — this multi-page <a href={withBase("docs/")}>docs</a> area, covering Getting Started, Capabilities, and Reference.</li>
      <li><strong>The <a href={withBase("docs/evals/")}>self-eval harness</a></strong> — decision-quality measures, controls, and a corrections log.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="prose__h">v0.1 → v0.1.2 — initial Agentry</h2>
    <p>
      The first releases established the core: a right-sized conductor, the SDLC specialist roster,
      durable memory, and the primer that warms a session.
    </p>

    <h3 class="prose__h prose__h--sub">Added</h3>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><strong>The right-sized conductor</strong> — routes a task to the least process that wins (one-shot → spec-first → decompose + verify).</li>
      <li><strong>The SDLC specialist roster</strong> — the explorer, architect, implementer, verifier, librarian, and the rest of the specialist agents.</li>
      <li><strong>The memory MCP</strong> — durable facts and episodes the conductor can recall, so run #2 is warmer than run #1. Replaced by <code>agentry mem</code> in 0.3.</li>
      <li><strong>The primer</strong> — a minimal session nudge that points the conductor at the repo's conventions and memory.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
